    "state": "Hawaii",
    "summary": "  You may have read about the recent case of State v Cramer 277 P3d 335 in which former Kamehameha Schools student and current high school junior Christopher Cramer was found guilty on charges relating to his violent conduct toward several classmates and two female teachers at King Middle School The court upheld the conviction but ordered a re sentence with one additional condition: that Mr Cramer not be permitted access to any computer or internet device while in state custody The Hawaii Supreme Court ruled Wednesday that requiring prison inmates who have been convicted of committing violent crimes against fellow prisoners and school children to refrain from using electronic devices is constitutional under the First Amendment but ordered the trial judge to explain why he decided differently for Mr Cramer In a majority opinion filed by Chief Judge Michael Reckmann Jr Justice Linares concurring in part and dissenting in part the Hawaii Supreme Court unanimously reversed Crammer's conviction on the school violence charge \u2014 also known as felony assault under Haw Rev Stat Ann 704 351 b 2008 \u2014 but ordered that sentence be carried out exactly as is written: The judge had sentenced Mr Cramer to a term of imprisonment and",
